## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-region sagas with per-tenant isolation, durable storage, and reliable cleanup.

## Key Concepts
- Saga orchestration across regions with CQRS and Event Sourcing
- Per-tenant event envelopes and outbox pattern
- Compensating actions and idempotent handlers
- Replay-safe projections and cross-region read-model updates

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal orchestrator sketch (pseudo)
function startSaga(tenantId, mediaId){
  const sagaId = uuid();
  persistSaga({id:sagaId, tenantId, mediaId, step:'Transcode', status:'in_progress'});
  publish({type:'Ingest', payload:{tenantId, mediaId, sagaId}});
}
function handleFailure(sagaId, failedStep){
  const comp = {Transcode:'DeleteTempArtifacts', PublishEU:'RevokePublishEU'}[failedStep];
  publish({type:'Compensate', payload:{sagaId, action:comp}});
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you ensure idempotency across services during retries?
- How would you observe and reconcile outbox vs. internal state across regions?

